  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Variation in Real Life 3 - Utility bill</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A water bill, \(C\), has a fixed standing charge plus a charge for each unit of water used: \(C = ku + b\), where \(u\) is the number of units used.</p>
<p>Using \({@pu1@}\) units costs \({@pC1@}\) Ksh. Using \({@pu2@}\) units costs \({@pC2@}\) Ksh.</p>
<p>(a) Find the rate per unit, \(k\).</p>
<p>\(k = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Find the fixed standing charge, \(b\).</p>
<p>\(b = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>

<p><strong>(a) Find the rate per unit \(k\)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: write an equation for each bill.</strong> Substitute each pair of values into \(C = ku + b\):</p>
\[ {@pC1@} = {@pu1@}k + b \qquad \text{(1)} \]
\[ {@pC2@} = {@pu2@}k + b \qquad \text{(2)} \]
<p><strong>Step 2: subtract equation (1) from equation (2).</strong> Both equations contain \(+\,b\), so subtracting them removes \(b\) and leaves only \(k\):</p>
\[ {@pC2@} - {@pC1@} = {@pu2@}k - {@pu1@}k \quad\Longrightarrow\quad {@pC2-pC1@} = {@pu2-pu1@}k. \]
<p>The extra \({@pu2-pu1@}\) units cost an extra Ksh \({@pC2-pC1@}\). The standing charge is the same on both bills, so it isn't part of this difference.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: divide both sides by \({@pu2-pu1@}\).</strong> \(k\) is multiplied by \({@pu2-pu1@}\), so dividing by \({@pu2-pu1@}\) leaves \(k\) on its own:</p>
\[ k = \frac{ {@pC2-pC1@} }{ {@pu2-pu1@} } = {@pk@}. \]
<p>So each unit of water costs Ksh \({@pk@}\).</p>

<p><strong>(b) Find the fixed standing charge \(b\)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: substitute \(k = {@pk@}\) into equation (1).</strong></p>
\[ {@pC1@} = {@pk@} \times {@pu1@} + b. \]
<p><strong>Step 2: multiply.</strong> \({@pk@} \times {@pu1@} = {@pk*pu1@}\), so</p>
\[ {@pC1@} = {@pk*pu1@} + b. \]
<p><strong>Step 3: subtract \({@pk*pu1@}\) from both sides.</strong></p>
\[ b = {@pC1@} - {@pk*pu1@} = {@pb@}. \]
<p>So the fixed standing charge is Ksh \({@pb@}\), paid every month however much water is used.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
